  "id": "Compound::DB00800 - Gene::150",
  "verbalization": "Fenoldopam exhibits a strong binding interaction with Adra2c, a variant of the Adrenergic Receptor, and this binding is linked to the participation of Adra2c in Alpha-2 adrenergic receptor signaling pathways. These pathways are central to the modulation of adrenergic signaling, which is a key mechanism in the regulation of physiological processes such as vascular tone and metabolic regulation. The evidence suggests that Fenoldopam may influence Adra2a through its interaction with Adra2c, which is part of a broader network of adrenergic receptor activity. The consistent presence of Adra2c in multiple pathways, including those involving Alpha2-adrenergic receptors, supports the hypothesis that Fenoldopam exerts its effects on Adra2a via a mechanism involving the activation or modulation of adrenergic receptor signaling. The integrated evidence from the three paths indicates a plausible, mechanistically grounded relationship between Fenoldopam and Adra2a, centered on the role of Adra2c in adrenergic receptor signaling.",
